### 20.7 Waste Management and Circular Economy Initiatives

- **Comprehensive Waste Reduction Strategies:**
  - Implementing a zero-waste policy across all operations, aimed at diverting at least 90% of waste from landfills through recycling, composting, and reuse initiatives. This involves auditing waste streams to identify key areas for reduction and establishing clear guidelines for waste segregation.
  - Partnering with local recycling facilities and composting organizations to ensure that materials are properly processed and repurposed. For instance, collaborating with city programs that focus on organic waste management can enhance our composting efforts and reduce methane emissions from landfills.

- **Upcycling and Reuse Programs:**
  - Encouraging employees and stakeholders to participate in upcycling initiatives that transform waste materials into new products. For example, hosting workshops where employees can learn to create usable items from scrap materials, ultimately fostering creativity and sustainability.
  - Establishing a “Reuse Marketplace” within the company, where employees can exchange items they no longer need, thus extending the lifecycle of products and reducing consumption.

